      "title": "X11: Fix GenericExtension dissection",
      "message": "X11: Fix GenericExtension dissection\n\nThe field adding macros already increment the offset pointer, so\nthe offset was getting double incremented for the GenericEvent\nlength and this never worked.\n\nThe generic macros don't return a tree item suitable for using\nto add an expert info, so don't use it here.\n\nCheck for overflow when transforming the event length on the wire\ninto the actual number of bytes.\n\nhttps://www.x.org/releases/X11R7.6/doc/xextproto/geproto.html\n\nFix #20717\n",
